            <ArticleTitle>[Association between gene polymorphism of CD40 gene and coronary artery lesion in Kawasaki disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1025-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To study the association between two single nucleotide polymorphisms (rs4810485 and rs1535045 in CD40 gene) and Kawasaki disease (KD) in Han Chinese children.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">A case-control study was performed on 184 children with KD and 206 normal controls. The polymorphisms of two SNPs in CD40 gene were detected using PCR-RFLP.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">There were no significant differences in the genotype distribution and allele frequency of SNP rs4810485 in CD40 gene between the KD and normal groups (P&amp;gt;0.05). The genotype distribution of SNP rs1535045 in CD40 gene in the KD group was significantly different from the control group (P&amp;lt;0.05). T allele of SNP rs1535045 was shown as a risk factor for development of KD (OR=1.592, 95%CI: 1.182-2.144, P=0.004). There were no association between the polymorphisms of the two SNPs and coronary artery lesions (P&amp;gt;0.05).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">SNP rs1535045 may be associated with the development of KD in Han Chinese children, while SNP rs4810485 may not.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
